					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="406" height="232" src="https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/bleachbit-logo-on-graphic-406x232.jpg" class="attachment-post-list size-post-list wp-post-image" alt="BleachBit app logo." decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/bleachbit-logo-on-graphic-406x232.jpg 406w, https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/bleachbit-logo-on-graphic-350x200.jpg 350w, https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/bleachbit-logo-on-graphic-840x480.jpg 840w" sizes="(max-width: 406px) 100vw, 406px" />BleachBit, the free, open-source and cross-platform system cleaning utility has a new maintenance release out – with support for Ubuntu 26.10. BleachBit 6.0.6 introduces cleaners for the Helium browser and Docker Desktop (including its AI assistant). This update also boosts app startup times, and makes deep scan, file deletion and file wiping faster, the latter now wiping in 512 KiB blocks rather than 4 KiB. A few preexisting cleaners now extend to more areas. Stale crash reports, GPU caches and session files for Claude, VS Code-based editors and Chromium can (optionally; variously) be expunged with this update. LibreWolf cleaning now [&#8230;]</p>
<p>You're reading <a href="https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk/2026/10/bleachbit-606-update-speed-boost">BleachBit 6.0.6 released with fixes for admin cleaning on Linux</a>, a blog post from <a href="https://www.omgubuntu.co.uk">OMG! Ubuntu</a>. Do not reproduce elsewhere without permission.</p>
]]></description>
		
